# Single source of truth for every pinned version.
# Values marked RESOLVED were extracted from the release manifest chart rather than the docs,
# because the install guide tells you to grep them out at install time which is not reproducible.

# --- BNK ---
BNK_VERSION=2.4.0
CNE_REPO=repo.f5.com
CNE_CHART=f5-bigip-k8s-manifest                     # the release manifest chart, used to resolve upgrade targets
# 2.4.0, not 2.3.0. On 2.3.0 the lifecycle operator cannot create the TMM DaemonSet at all: it logs
# "Adding TMM TMM_K8S_ROUTES environment variables" and panics in the same millisecond with
# "assignment to entry in nil map" at f5tmm_daemonset.go:186, which aborts the build. An existing
# DaemonSet survives it, so a long lived cluster looks healthy while a fresh install never gets TMM.
# Reproduced by deleting the DaemonSet on a working 2.3.0 cluster and watching it fail to return, and
# not fixed by v2.21.13-0.0.64, by TMM_K8S_ROUTE=false, by placement.dataPlane.nodeSelector, by
# creating the missing configmap, or by restarting the operator.
#
# 2.4.0 ships f5-lifecycle-operator v2.30.0-0.5.2, which runs the same code path with zero panics and
# creates the DaemonSet. Verified on a real cluster before pinning it here.
CNE_RELEASE_MANIFEST=2.4.0                          # 86 pinned components
# 2.4.0, not 2.4.0-3.3175.0-0.0.380. The registry carries both tags and only the short one is what the
# operator resolves. With the long form it logs "Manifest version not found, retrieving from remote
# registry" then "Unable to retrieve remote manifest, ensure manifest exists in registry or create the
# required CNEManifest resource", and the CNEInstance sits at Reconciled=False with one pod and no
# errors anywhere else, which is a very quiet way to fail. 2.3.0 used the long form, so the format
# changed between releases.
FLO_VERSION=v2.30.0-0.5.2                          # RESOLVED charts/f5-lifecycle-operator
CERT_GEN_VERSION=0.9.3                             # RESOLVED utils/f5-cert-gen
TMM_CHART_VERSION=15.1016.2-0.4.137                # RESOLVED charts/f5-tmm

# --- cluster prerequisites ---
K8S_MINOR=1.30
CALICO_VERSION=v3.29.1
CERT_MANAGER_VERSION=v1.16.2
MULTUS_VERSION=v4.2.0
SRIOV_DP_VERSION=v3.10.0                           # DPU profile only

# --- lint toolchain, pinned so local and CI report identically ---
# Distro shellcheck differs between a developer box and a runner, and findings differ with it.
# 0.9.0 reports SC2002 where 0.11.0 does not, which is exactly the kind of drift this prevents.
SHELLCHECK_VERSION=v0.11.0
ACTIONLINT_VERSION=v1.7.12

# --- install targets ---
NS_CORE=f5-cne-core
NS_BNK=f5-bnk
CLUSTER_ISSUER=f5-cne-internal-ca
CA_COMMON_NAME=f5-cne-internal-ca-root             # MUST differ from leaf CNs or CWC x509 fails
MULTUS_MEMORY_LIMIT=512Mi                          # BNK floods Multus, default limit OOMKills
